==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|diversite}}, from {{der|en|fro|diversité}}, from {{uder|en|la|dīversitās}}. Displaced native {{ncog|ang|mislīcnes}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/daɪˈvɜː(ɹ)sɪti/|/dɪˈvɜː(ɹ)sɪti/}}
* {{audio|en|en-uk-diversity.ogg|a=UK}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The quality of being [[diverse]] or [[different]]; [[difference]] or [[unlikeness]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:nonuniformity}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1971|author=w:Lyndon Johnson|chapter="I feel like I have already been here a year"|title=w:The Vantage Point|url=https://archive.org/details/vantagepointpers00john/|publisher=w:Holt, Reinhart & Winston|ISBN=0-03-084492-4|LCCN=74-102146|OCLC=1067880747|page=23|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/vantagepointpers00john/page/23/|text=On December 17 I addressed the UN General Assembly, stating that it was this nation's policy to help create a world that "can be safe for '''diversity''' and free from hostility."}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Caroline Davies; Emily Dugan|title=Coronation aimed for diversity but real challenges still lie ahead|work=The Guardian|date=2023-05-07|url=https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2023/may/07/coronation-aimed-for-diversity-but-real-challenges-still-lie-ahead|issn=0261-3077|quotee=w:Adjoa Andoh|passage=One place there were none, of course, was on the Buckingham Palace balcony, as was observed by the Bridgerton actor Adjoa Andoh – who contrasted on the ITV coverage “the rich '''diversity''' of the abbey” and “a terribly white balcony”.}}
# A [[variety]]; [[diverse]] types or examples.
#: {{syn|en|selection}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=6 Aug 83 |journal=Gay Community News|page=15|author=Rob Schmieder|title=Disco Consumers And Rock Activists|text=Hendryx has laid down eight tracks that flow seamlessly through funk, disco, gospel, rock and reggae, with nary a false step along the way. She is at home in this '''diversity''' of styles because she has paid her dues in all of them: from her days as one of the dynamoes of Labelle through collaborations with rock band Talking Heads, funk band Cameo {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-07-26|author=[http://www.theguardian.com/profile/nick-miroff Nick Miroff]
|volume=189|issue=7|page=32|magazine=w:The Guardian Weekly
|title=[http://www.theguardian.com/world/2013/jul/23/mexico-insect-cuisine-sustainable-food Mexico gets a taste for eating insects&nbsp;&hellip;]
|passage=The San Juan market is Mexico City's most famous deli of exotic meats, where an adventurous shopper can hunt down hard-to-find critters such as ostrich, wild boar and crocodile. Only the city zoo offers greater species '''diversity'''.}}
# {{lb|en|mostly|business}} [[equal-opportunity|Equal-opportunity]] [[inclusion]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2003|author=Adalberto Aguirre|title=Racial and Ethnic Diversity in America: A Reference Handbook|page=72
|passage=Bakke has shaped a precarious context for '''diversity''' initiatives in higher education. On the one hand, the U.S. Supreme Court has reasoned that race may serve a purpose in the admissions process; however, race may not be used as a corrective measure, such as by establishing quotas.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Jay Caspian Kang|title=Can We Talk About Critical Race Theory?|work=The New York Times|date=2021-11-11|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2021/11/11/opinion/critical-race-theory.html|issn=0362-4331|passage='''Diversity''' is now a big industry — about $8 billion per year gets spent on '''diversity''' trainings in America — and parents might be feeling blindsided by the rapid changes, many of which came after last year’s George Floyd protests.}}

